    <body n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0460.didymoi.meineke1841-grc1" xml:lang="grc">
      <div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0460.didymoi.meineke1841-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0460_didymoi">
        <head>ΔΙΔΥΜΟΙ</head>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-1">
          <head>I.</head>
          <lg>
            <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-1-l1">Qui se nepotans rebus evolvit suis,</l>
            <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-1-l2">aliena recte quomodo curet bona?</l>
          </lg>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1_2" ana="#compiled-duplicate-number #compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-1_2">
          <lg>
            <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-1_2-l1">Ὁ γὰρ τὸν ἴδιον οἰκονομῶν κακῶς βίον,</l>
            <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-1_2-l2">πῶς οὗτος ἂν σώσειε τῶν ἔξω τινά;</l>
          </lg>
          <note type="source">Stobaeus Flor. XV 2 cum lemmate Εὔφρονος Διδύμων. „Sic Froben. Εὔφρονος B. Nihil enotavi ex A. Εὔφρονος ἐν Διδύμοις Schow. Euphronis in Didymis Gesner. Euphro Geminis Grotius.“ Gaisfordus.</note>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="2" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-2">
          <head>II.</head>
          <lg>
            <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-2-l1">Cum tam breve aevum tribuas nobis, Iuppiter,</l>
            <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-2-l2">cur sine dolore hoc non permittis degere?</l>
          </lg>
        </div>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="2_2" ana="#compiled-duplicate-number #compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-2_2">
          <lg>
            <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-2_2-l1">Ὦ Ζεῦ, τί ποθ᾽ ἡμῖν δοὺς χρόνον τοῦ ζῆν βραχύν</l>
            <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0460-didymoi-2_2-l2">πλέκειν ἀλύπως τοῦτον ἡμᾶς οὐκ ἐᾶς;</l>
          </lg>
          <note type="source">Stobaeus Flor. XCVIII 42 cum lemmate Εὔφρονος Διδύμων. Versu primo A πάνθ᾽ pro ποθ᾽.</note>
        </div>
      </div>
